WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.560
The outer terminal moraine marks the farthest position of this

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:04.300
advance.

00:00:04.905 --> 00:00:08.445
As ice retreats, pauses can leave curved recessional ridges

00:00:08.445 --> 00:00:09.625
inside it.

00:00:09.845 --> 00:00:13.485
Under moving ice, elongated drumlins can record the flow

00:00:13.485 --> 00:00:14.325
trend.

00:00:14.985 --> 00:00:18.325
A meltwater channel inside or beneath the ice leaves a winding

00:00:18.325 --> 00:00:20.445
esker after the ice disappears.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.520
Streams spread outwash in front.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:28.050
A detached ice block buried by sediment can melt away, leaving

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:29.010
a kettle.

00:00:29.405 --> 00:00:32.165
Water may later fill the hollow.
